            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0121" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.9411/321: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-27T18:00:00+02:00">November 27,
                            1941—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 28—2:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>613. An exchange of telegrams between Hitler and Ryti is published in the Finnish
                    press this morning. Hitler is reported to have telegraphed to the President: <pb
                        facs="0122" n="110" xml:id="pg110"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In consequence of Finland’s recent adherence to the pact against
                            Communist International, I beg to express my heartfelt wishes for the
                            happiness and success of Your Excellency and the Finnish nation as a
                            whole.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>In the Finnish press President Ryti’s telegram to Hitler is reported as follows:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“For the cordial telegram which Your Excellency sent me in consequence of
                            Finland’s adherence to the Anti-Comintern Pact, the object of which is
                            to deliver all peoples from Communist menace, I wish hereby on behalf of
                            myself and of the Finnish people to express my sincere thanks and to
                            extend at the same time my warmest wishes for the happiness and success
                            of the heroic German people.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>However, the text of the latter message in the suspended language papers is
                    slightly different: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“… I wish to express on behalf of myself and the Finnish people my
                            sincere gratitude and at the same time to present my warmest
                            felicitations to Your Excellency and the heroic German people and to
                            wish it happiness and success.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
